{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpret the corrected execution (CheckRun 4dc33f26f12e4cd69f7aae09af6c1ee6, fixed experiment c3dd9a52a0c44b21af5b3204cf642efb-experiment, version 2) and supersede the earlier, tainted receipt: all six comparisons resolved - the two controls hold, both witness-event premises hold, and the two witness assertions are violated. Because this basis honours the application's persistence duty, the account returns from conditional to violated, and the earlier receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d is withdrawn as evidence for the witness while its conclusion is preserved in history.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"c3dd9a52a0c44b21af5b3204cf642efb-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"4dc33f26f12e4cd69f7aae09af6c1ee6\\\":[1,4],\\\"8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d\\\":[1,2,3,4]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The account is execution-backed again, now on a prefix that honours the application's duties. Source side: node.run sets its proposal channel to nil when an applied configuration change removes the local node from Progress and the node appears in neither cs.Voters nor cs.VotersOutgoing (node.go:400-432), restores the channel from n.propc only in the branch that reacts to a change of r.lead with a leader known (node.go:343-380), and Node.Propose sends into that channel, so a nil channel makes the call wait for the caller's context or the node's done channel (node.go:514-551); the target's own comment calls the reset unsound (node.go:409-411) and the only documented caveat is that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140). Receipt 4dc33f26f12e4cd69f7aae09af6c1ee6 (five parsed events, no loss, six comparisons all resolved) shows a conforming sequence: the wrapped node applies the bootstrap entry, the removal and the re-add in order (parsed events 0-3 carry applied/committed 1, 2, 3 and 4 with the leader's configuration moving voters=(1 2) -> voters=(1) -> voters=(1 2)), while the same term and the same known leader 1 persist throughout. Controls: before the removal Propose returns no error in 0ms and the leader's log index is 2 (parsed index 1, both comparisons hold), so the wrapper forwards a follower's proposal to its leader. Witness: after the re-add - with the leader's configuration containing node 2 again (premise comparison holds at parsed index 4) and the node still knowing leader 1 (premise comparison holds) - Propose returns only when its 300ms context deadline fires and the leader's log index stays at 4 (both witness comparisons violated with a complete witness). The defect statement is therefore: a node that the application has added back to the configuration, and that knows the leader of that configuration in the same term, cannot hand a proposal to raft through the Node interface; the wrapper holds the call until the caller's context expires, and the proposal never reaches the group. The only mechanism the source leaves for re-opening the channel is a leadership change, which does not occur in this state, so the affected duty is lost until the application stops using that node, the leadership changes, or the application switches to RawNode (which is unaffected because it has no proposal channel of its own). The earlier receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d is kept in history but withdrawn as evidence for the witness: its prefix omitted the application's persistence duty, and this successor re-measured the same control, premises and witness on the corrected prefix.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The controls hold in the corrected receipt (parsed index 1): the same call before the removal returns no error and the leader's log index advances, so the blocked behaviour is specific to the state after the removal and the re-add.\\\",\n   \\\"The Node.Propose documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice and that retries are the caller's job (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the specific defect is that the channel stays closed while the node is a member again and a leader is known, which that warning does not describe.\\\",\n   \\\"The corrected receipt supersedes rather than refutes the suspicious behaviour of the earlier receipt: the earlier run's prefix (entries never written to storage before Advance) is not a conforming application prefix, and the behaviour reproduced unchanged once that duty was honoured.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process; the leader is installed directly and broadcasts its appends.\\\",\n   \\\"The proposed call uses a 300ms deadline: the receipt measures that the call did not complete within it and that the group's log did not change, not the absolute duration of the closed channel.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path named in the question's discriminator remains unmeasured, and the diagnostic attempt was removed from the harness because it hung the run (the node's run loop stopped servicing status requests after the witness).\\\",\n   \\\"Whether an application is expected to keep proposing through a node that has been removed and re-added is itself part of the question; the library's own comment calls the mechanism unsound rather than documenting an intended semantics.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update21.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update21.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
