{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='update21.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['interpretations'][0]['joint_history']=\\\"Both receipts are the same harness family, scenario, fixture and observation set: a wrapped node 2 and a bare leader 1 over storages with voters {1,2}, the same propose/apply sequence (removal of node 2, then re-add), the same Propose call with a 300ms deadline, the same status-channel snapshots, and the same decisive endpoints (Propose's return value and duration, the leader's log index around the call). Receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d is the earlier basis whose pump never wrote Ready.Entries to that node's storage, so its prefix was not a conforming application prefix and its witness is withdrawn as evidence; receipt 4dc33f26f12e4cd69f7aae09af6c1ee6 is the successor basis whose pump persists entries, hard state and snapshots before sending and advancing, and it re-measured the same control, the same premises (now as completed comparisons on the witness event) and the same witness. The successor's indices 1 and 4 therefore carry the same meaning as the earlier receipt's indices 1 and 4, with the earlier one no longer relied upon.\\\"\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update21.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
